# Overseer checkpoint contract — {{ id }}

This file is generated per-run and is AUTHORITATIVE for every emitting task in this workflow
(`intake` and every `ck-JJ` checkpoint). Copy ids, paths, and shapes from here LITERALLY,
substituting only `<slug>` (a short kebab-case description you choose) and the numeric wave/
checkpoint segments shown as concrete examples below. Every rule in "Hard rules" below applies
to the manifest and verdict you emit — a violation fails your checkpoint task and halts the run
(resumable). This is a forward-looking contract: the checkpoint's manifest and verdict must
satisfy every rule below, whether or not the checker that enforces a given rule has landed yet
(see "Hard rules" for which are enforced by the shipped tool today versus forthcoming).

## Paths for this run

- Instance dir (workspace-relative): `{{ instance_dir }}`
- Instance dir (absolute):           `{{ workspace_root }}/{{ instance_dir }}`
- Outputs dir:                       `{{ instance_dir }}/outputs`
- Control dir (hold/override files): `{{ instance_dir }}/control`
- Tool path (absolute, every hook invokes this): `{{ workspace_root }}/{{ instance_dir }}/tools/overseer_tool.py`
- Config:                            `{{ instance_dir }}/overseer-config.json`
- Charter (locked at intake):        `{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/charter.json`
- Ledger (tool-owned, append-only):  `{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/ledger.jsonl`

## Id patterns

- **Wave units**: `wJJ-NN-<slug>` — `JJ` is the zero-padded wave number, `NN` the zero-padded
  unit number within that wave, `<slug>` a short kebab-case description of the unit's work.
- **Checkpoints**: `ck-JJ` — zero-padded, `ck-JJ` reviews wave `JJ` (e.g. `ck-01` reviews
  wave 1's units).
- **Fixed tail ids** (never reused, never renamed): `final-verify`, `closeout`, `final-push`.
- **Expander patterns** (FR-15 — only relevant if `max_expanders_per_wave` > 0; this run's
  `max_expanders_per_wave` is `{{ params.max_expanders_per_wave }}`, and FR-15 is off by
  default and **not yet implemented in this epic** — see `T-zLHc7Q`, deferred; do not emit a
  `kind: expand` unit while it reads 0): expander leaves are `<unit-id>--NN-<slug>`, and the
  fixed sub-aggregator is `<unit-id>--done`.

## Emitted-entry shapes

Every entry you emit is a `tasks[]` item in your `task_manifest_path` JSON (strict JSON,
`{"tasks": [...]}`, no comments, no trailing commas). The examples below follow one run's story
end to end: `intake` emits wave 1 (`w01-*`) plus `ck-01`; `ck-01` in turn either continues with
another wave, or emits the close-out tail. Substitute `<slug>` with your own short kebab-case
token; every other field is copied literally.

### Unit (kind ∈ `{research, design, implement, test, review, fix, document, verify, stabilize}`)

```json
{"id": "w01-01-<slug>", "agent": "developer",
 "instruction": "workflows/overseer-runner/instructions/10-work-unit.md",
 "depends_on": ["intake"],
 "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/overseer-contract.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/charter.json",
            "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/waves/w01/briefs/w01-01-<slug>.json"],
 "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/waves/w01/w01-01-<slug>.md",
             "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/progress/w01-01-<slug>.json"],
 "pre_hook": {"use": "ov-unit-gate"},
 "timeout_seconds": 7200, "skip_if_outputs_exist": true, "effort": "medium"}
```

`agent` and `instruction` come from the kind→agent/instruction map below and must match it
**exactly** (OV-R6) — the example above shows `kind: implement` → `developer`. `depends_on` must
include the emitter (`intake`, or the previous `ck-JJ` for a later wave) and may otherwise only
reference other ids in this same manifest (OV-R8). A unit may also carry optional
`"touches": [...]` (best-effort glob hints) and/or `"isolation": "none"|"worktree"|"inherit"`
(both omitted by default) — see `TaskSpec` for the full optional-field set; do not add fields
beyond `id, agent, instruction, depends_on, inputs, outputs, pre_hook, timeout_seconds,
skip_if_outputs_exist, effort, touches, isolation` (OV-R2/OV-R9 — no `post_hook`, no `model`, no
`max_turns` on a unit).

### Next checkpoint

```json
{"id": "ck-01", "agent": "manager", "instruction": "workflows/overseer-runner/instructions/20-checkpoint.md",
 "depends_on": ["w01-01-<slug>", "w01-02-<slug>"],
 "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/overseer-contract.md", "{{ instance_dir }}/overseer-config.json",
            "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/charter.json",
            "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/progress/w01-01-<slug>.json",
            "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/progress/w01-02-<slug>.json"],
 "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/checkpoints/ck-01/digest.json",
             "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/checkpoints/ck-01/verdict.json",
             "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/checkpoints/ck-01/report.md"],
 "emit_tasks": true, "task_manifest_path": "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/manifests/ck-01.json",
 "pre_hook": {"use": "ov-ckpt-prep"}, "post_hook": {"use": "ov-ckpt-check", "on_failure": "fail_task"},
 "timeout_seconds": 3600, "skip_if_outputs_exist": false, "effort": "{{ params.overseer_effort }}"}
```

`depends_on` must list **every** unit id in this manifest (or expander `--done` ids), or `[<the
emitter's own id>]` when the wave is empty — that is exactly the **hold** shape: decision `hold`
emits the next checkpoint with zero wave units and `depends_on` set to only the emitter. `inputs`
must include every unit's (and every expander's `--done`) breadcrumb path. See "The
`overseer_model` rule" below for when this entry must also carry `"model"`.

### Tail (terminal emission only — emitted instead of a next checkpoint, never alongside one)

```json
[
  {"id": "final-verify", "agent": "tester", "instruction": "workflows/overseer-runner/instructions/40-final-verify.md",
   "depends_on": ["ck-01"],
   "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/charter.json", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/checkpoints/ck-01/verdict.json"],
   "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/final/verify.md"], "timeout_seconds": 7200, "skip_if_outputs_exist": false},
  {"id": "closeout", "agent": "manager", "instruction": "workflows/overseer-runner/instructions/41-closeout.md",
   "depends_on": ["final-verify"],
   "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/charter.json", "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/final/verify.md"],
   "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/final/closeout.md"], "timeout_seconds": 3600, "skip_if_outputs_exist": false},
  {"id": "final-push", "agent": "git-operator", "instruction": "workflows/overseer-runner/instructions/90-final-push.md",
   "depends_on": ["closeout"],
   "inputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/final/closeout.md"],
   "outputs": ["{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/final/push-report.md"], "timeout_seconds": 2400,
   "skip_if_outputs_exist": false, "isolation": "none"}
]
```

Emit all three ids exactly as shown, with `depends_on` chained `final-verify → closeout →
final-push` and the first entry's `depends_on` set to the emitting checkpoint's own id.
`final-push` is included **iff** `final_push` is true for this run (this run's `final_push` is
`{{ params.final_push }}`); when it is false, emit only `final-verify` and `closeout`. There is
no static tail task in this workflow — see this template's `README.md` ("The DAG shape") for why.

### Expander (FR-15 — deferred, do not emit while `max_expanders_per_wave` reads 0 above)

A unit whose brief sets `"kind": "expand"` is itself `"emit_tasks": true` with its own
`"task_manifest_path": "{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/manifests/<unit-id>.json"` and
`"post_hook": {"use": "ov-expander-check", "on_failure": "fail_task"}`, `agent: "architect"`,
`instruction: "workflows/overseer-runner/instructions/30-expander.md"`. Its own manifest holds
at most `sub_wave_size` leaves (`<unit-id>--NN-<slug>`, the ordinary unit shape, never
`emit_tasks`) plus exactly one `<unit-id>--done` (agent `manager`, instruction
`31-sub-aggregate.md`, `depends_on` every leaf, outputs
`{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/waves/wJJ/<unit-id>--done.md` and
`{{ instance_dir }}/outputs/progress/<unit-id>--done.json`). **This kind is not yet wired up in
this epic — leave `max_expanders_per_wave` at 0 and never emit `kind: expand` until a later
task documents enabling it.**

